{
  "_note": "What Fallout 4 1.10.163 actually did with this project's scripts on the owner's PC, as reported back (docs/design/VERIFY_LOG.md). tools/papyrus_sim/test_sim.py replays each run in the stand-in engine, with the scripts as they were at that commit, and fails if the stand-in gives a different result. Add a run here only from a real report; never edit a number to make a test pass. From the eleventh run on, a scenario also records the lines the main quest's timing guards wrote to the script log (guard_lines; the report lists them for the whole run, so an empty list is a recorded fact too) and, where a case notes it, whether two handlers overlapped (overlap). A key that begins stand_in_ is not a fact about the game: it tells the replay which of the stand-in's modes to use. Scenario 132 of the eleventh run overlapped in the game, which the stand-in's ordinary mode cannot do at all; it is replayed with every call taking a frame, and the number of tenths waited is then not compared, because that mode provokes overlaps and predicts no timings.",
